WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.112
Vendors teach their products,

2
00:00:02.112 --> 00:00:05.825
and Book 16 names them as
examples, never endorsements.

3
00:00:05.825 --> 00:00:10.373
A vendor course earns a place only if it
maps to a book procedure, it's current,

4
00:00:10.373 --> 00:00:12.940
the agency can keep the completion record,

5
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.387
and the agency knows how the
vendor handles learner data.

6
00:00:16.387 --> 00:00:19.261
That record point matters,
because exam records

7
00:00:19.261 --> 00:00:22.350
tied to a work account vanish
when the person leaves.

8
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.937
Lab environments are harder to
get than most programs expect.

9
00:00:25.937 --> 00:00:27.663
The free sandboxes are gone,

10
00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:31.638
and the developer sandbox isn't
offered in any government cloud.

11
00:00:31.638 --> 00:00:35.586
So the program office arranges lab
tenants, and before each gate the

12
00:00:35.586 --> 00:00:39.887
team rehearses once in the agency's
own non-production government tenant.

13
00:00:39.887 --> 00:00:44.208
And every lab follows the same rules,
starting with never production,

14
00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:47.088
synthetic data only, and
tear it down at the end.

15
00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:48.600
Now, everyone else.
